+### Offline design review package filenames
+
+An offline Design Review Package (DRP) uses one package stem across its
+drafts and accepted Final documents. A package is design material for the
+Architecture Review lifecycle. The HCRL records standing and disposition.
+Filename versions belong to the DRP and are independent of Architecture,
+software and HCRL versions.
+
+- `DRP-<package>.Draft.NNN.III.md` identifies a draft. `NNN` is the immediately
+  preceding accepted Final version for that package, or `000` before its first
+  accepted Final. `III` is the positive draft iteration, beginning at `001`
+  for each baseline.
+- `DRP-<package>.Final.NNN.md` identifies a resulting accepted DRP version.
+  Use three decimal digits, with the first Final numbered `001` and each
+  subsequent Final numbered one above the preceding Final. Use the
+  case-sensitive spellings `Draft` and `Final`.
+- On attributable Solution Architect acceptance of the exact design, preserve
+  the reviewed draft, its disposition, qualifications and provenance. Use the
+  resulting Final number alone in the Final filename. For example,
+  `Draft.000.002` can lead to `Final.001`, after which drafting begins at
+  `Draft.001.001`. Acceptance of `Draft.001.002` can lead to `Final.002`;
+  its first successor draft is `Draft.002.001`.
+- Reconcile historical filenames through a bounded reviewed mapping.
+  Record old and corrected locators, accepted standing and exact source
+  correspondence. Preserve historical evidence and its references. Where
+  historical references need the old path, retain an explicitly documented
+  compatibility locator that preserves the required bytes or sections. Use
+  the corrected locator for new primary references after authorised
+  application. Historical reconciliation creates no new acceptance event.
+- Check names on submitted DRP candidates and report historical exceptions
+  for separate disposition. Validate baseline, sequence and Final standing
+  against attributable review records as part of Architecture Review.
+
